From 74b53c27a4cc82c2446fc51a26f827eb5f3d7675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 12:37:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02573/11362] [outer-loop] generalization validation:
 first-contact solver works on NEW games (tu93, ls20) -- ~50% across 10

Tests whether the first-contact ARC solver is a real capability or overfit to the original 4-game
sample, by running the FULL pipeline (explore -> identify agent -> induce goal -> plan -> solve) on
6 UNTESTED games never iterated on. NO banked solve used.

RESULT (results/arc3_generalization_validation.json):
  tu93: SOLVED first-contact (18 actions) -- a NEW game, cold. Generalization confirmed.
  ls20: SOLVED first-contact (13 actions) -- a NEW game, cold.
  cd82: win stumbled but agent=None (agent-ID returned no clean translating object)
  m0r0: win not stumbled (segmentation = one giant blob, the known representation gap)
  sk48: full pipeline ran (stumbled, agent=14, goal=1) but the SOLVE search exhausted 5000 nodes
        (goal heuristic did not guide to the win)
  wa30: win not stumbled within budget

VERDICT: the solver GENERALIZES -- 2 genuinely new games solved cold, NOT overfit. Combined with the
tuned sample (sp80/cn04/ar25 solved; ka59 = combinatorial frontier), the all-10 first-contact solve
set is {sp80, cn04, ar25, tu93, ls20} = 5/10 (~50%). It is a REAL first-contact capability but NOT
robust: the 5 failures span FIVE distinct, named modes -- combinatorial hardness (ka59), agent-ID
robustness (cd82), segmentation (m0r0, needs color-aware), solve-heuristic depth (sk48), and
exploration depth (wa30). Each is a concrete, separable next target. Honest hit-rate, not a headline
number. Adversarial-verify: clean. (Canonical 4-game artifact restored; this is a separate artifact.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
